## Part III — Execution Without a Global Clock: Cubical Interaction Nets

### 3.1 The Primitive Law of Interaction

Traditional proof assistants (Coq, Agda, Lean) evaluate terms on sequential, pointer-chasing runtimes with global heaps and stop-the-world garbage collectors. Hyperactivity's runtime (`src/net.c`) executes cubical terms directly as **Lafont interaction nets** (1990).

There is no global clock, no call stack, and no global mutable memory. A term is a graph of **cells** connected by **wires**:
- Every cell has one **principal port** and zero or more **auxiliary ports**.
- Cells have two polarities: **Values** ($\lambda$, pair, constructor, type, interval point, system, Glue) and **Operations** (apply, fst, snd, path-apply, compose, case, subst, duplicate, erase).
- An **active pair** occurs whenever an Operation's principal port meets a Value's principal port head-to-head.

A **step** removes those two cells and replaces them with a small local net wired to their open ports. Nothing else in the graph is inspected or locked:

- `apply(arg) ⋈ λ(x. body)` $\longrightarrow$ wire `arg` directly to `x`, wire `body` to output.
- `path-apply(r) ⋈ path-λ(i. t)` $\longrightarrow$ spawn a local dimension-substitution cell `subst[i := r]` facing `t`.
- `duplicate ⋈ value(parts)` $\longrightarrow$ hold the value once and give both consumers a reference (lazy sharing — subexpressions are never recomputed).
- `erase ⋈ value(parts)` $\longrightarrow$ delete the cell and send `erase` to each part (local reclamation with zero garbage-collector pauses).

### 3.2 Confluence and Heterogeneous GPU Parallelism

Because active pairs only touch their own two cells, **disjoint active pairs anywhere in the graph can fire simultaneously with zero locks**, and by strong confluence, the final normal form is guaranteed identical regardless of execution order.

This is the exact same computational primitive behind massively parallel GPU interaction-net runtimes (such as HVM/Bend). Unlike sequential proof checkers, Hyperactivity's execution model maps natively onto heterogeneous multi-core CPUs and GPUs: formal mathematical identity search, proof checking, and data transformation all share one lock-free parallel reduction engine.

### 3.3 Content-Addressed Exchange and No Canonical State

Every definition, proof, and document in Hyperactivity lives in an immutable content-addressed pool (`store/<sha256>/`), never mutated in place. There is **no global namespace and no canonical state**:
- A participant's local workspace is simply a root hash mapping human labels to immutable object hashes.
- Exchanging work with a peer means sending an object together with its cryptographic dependency closure and machine-checked proofs. The recipient verifies it locally and merges pools by **set union**.
- Because set union is **commutative, associative, and idempotent**, every pair of peers converges to the exact same verified pool regardless of message order — eliminating merge conflicts, package-registry gatekeepers, and platform lock-in at the root.

