## Part IV — Real Systems: Lifting, Specialization, and Post-Financial Credit

### 4.1 Every Existing Language Inside One Host (Zero Rewrite)

A foundational system cannot demand that the world rewrite billions of lines of existing C++, Rust, OCaml, or x86 assembly. In Hyperactivity, **a programming language is a value of the host**:
- `lib/cxx/` models C++ syntax and machine semantics.
- `lib/lang/rust/` models Rust places, rvalues, and ownership semantics.
- `lib/isa/x86/` formalizes x86-64 instructions, registers, flags, addressing, paging, and segmentation.
- `lib/isa/tso.cub` and `lib/mem/rc11.cub` formalize x86 Total Store Order and C/C++11 relaxed/acquire-release weak memory models as relations on memory events.

Existing production code is **lifted** into Hyperactivity with its exact semantics (including undefined behavior and concurrency) intact. Specifications and invariants attach directly to the lifted source object, and proofs erase cleanly back to native code. Enterprises and trading firms adopt verified execution **without rewriting a single legacy service**.

### 4.2 Verified Specialization and C-First Lowering

In `lib/specialize.cub` and Part I §6.2 & §9.4, **partial evaluation (specialization)** takes a general program and known static context (a protocol schema, hardware topology, or market-data format) and returns a **dependent pair**:

$$\big(\;\text{residual program } p',\; \text{proof path } p' \equiv p(\text{ctx})\;\big)$$

Optimization is admitted **only with its machine-checked equivalence proof**. For native execution, Hyperactivity uses **C-first lowering** (§9.4): verified residual programs lower to clean C whose source-to-C correctness relation composes with the downstream C compiler's relation to target machine code. Proof overhead vanishes on the hot path while the end-to-end refinement theorem remains intact.

### 4.3 Post-Financial Technology: Conserved Credit Without a Blockchain

In 1945, Friedrich Hayek argued that economies require scalar prices because dispersed human knowledge cannot be directly communicated or composed; a 1-dimensional price acts as a lossy summary signal. **Bitcoin (2009)** decentralized *who maintains the ledger*, but **kept the 1-dimensional scalar** — still erasing provenance, dependency structure, and evidence while paying global-consensus overhead to maintain one canonical state.

Hyperactivity's `lib/credit.cub` (Part I §10.3) replaces the scalar bottleneck with **conserved credit over local transitions**:
- Credit is held by peers and carried by messages in flight; local **allocation** and **delivery** transitions cancel identically so total credit is proved conserved across **every finite sequence of transitions**, with **no global scheduler and no global blockchain**.
- Each participant's compatible global states form an **observation fiber**, telling that peer exactly what its local receipts warrant.
- Combined with receipt-bearing idempotent delivery and full credit flowing along content-addressed dependency graphs without decay, dispersed knowledge and provenance compose directly — freeing information flows for optimal human coordination.

